{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgV8pGu3qEV2pstBoHECS", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CUsb3fZLgFm7yF4ToMxi4J", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to orders (`0.0825`, i.e. 8.25%).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for one order line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples, sums the line\n  totals, applies `TAX_RATE`, and returns the result rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns `order_total_amount - amount`, the\n  balance remaining after refunding `amount`.\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # 25.5 plus tax -> 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 5.00)               # 22.6\n```\nEOF\nawk 'length>=100' README.md; python3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import *\nt=order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]);print(t,refund(t,5))\""}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 474, "cache_read_input_tokens": 38168, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 474}, "output_tokens": 20, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T18:49:03.338Z", "request_id": "req_011CgV8pGRX8jjVS3qiyLwn5", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01CUsb3fZLgFm7yF4ToMxi4J": {"command": "cd /tmp/skilldiff-sgm36o9f/ws && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to orders (`0.0825`, i.e. 8.25%).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for one order line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples, sums the line\n  totals, applies `TAX_RATE`, and returns the result rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns `order_total_amount - amount`, the\n  balance remaining after refunding `amount`.\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # 25.5 plus tax -> 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 5.00)               # 22.6\n```\nEOF\nawk 'length>=100' README.md; python3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import *\nt=order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]);print(t,refund(t,5))\""}}, "wire_ingest_context": {"toolu_01CUsb3fZLgFm7yF4ToMxi4J": {"cwd": "/tmp/skilldiff-sgm36o9f/ws"}}}
